# ── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
master.key

# ── Go ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/bin/
/dist/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.test
*.prof
/hangar
/hangar.exe
# PHASE 23. A stray 71 MB dev build, `hangar.exe~`, was committed in Phase
# 20.7 and survived to the first public push, where GitHub flagged it. The
# pattern above is anchored and exact, so the editor-backup spelling slipped
# past it. Both are covered now.
hangar.exe*
*.exe~

# ── SPA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
web/node_modules/
# web/dist/ holds the Vite build output, which embed.FS needs present at Go
# build time (see web/embed.go). Ignore everything real `pnpm run build`
# produces, but keep the tracked .gitkeep placeholder so a fresh checkout can
# `go build`/`go test` before Node ever runs. A real local build empties this
# directory (vite emptyOutDir) and will show .gitkeep as locally deleted —
# expected, not a problem: CI/Docker builds from a fresh checkout each time.
web/dist/*
!web/dist/.gitkeep
web/.vite/
web/stats.html

# Playwright run artefacts (Phase 18). The suite itself lives in web/e2e/ and
# is tracked; these are per-run outputs — traces, screenshots, HTML reports —
# and are regenerated by every `pnpm run e2e`.
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
web/blob-report/
web/.playwright/
web/playwright-report/
web/test-results/

# ── generated, but COMMITTED on purpose ──────────────────────────────────────
# internal/store/gen/, docs/openapi.json and web/src/api/schema.d.ts are
# generated AND tracked: Principle 10 requires CI to diff them so a schema drift
# is a build failure rather than a runtime surprise. Do not add them here.

# ── the Gate 7 corpus recorder's vendored legacy sources ─────────────────────
# testdata/legacy-api-v2/recorder/ is committed BECAUSE the recording has to be
# reproducible, but the four eveseat repositories it runs are NOT vendored here:
# they are cloned at the exact commits testdata/legacy-api-v2/README.md pins,
# which is what makes the pin verifiable rather than a claim about a directory
# somebody could have edited. Same for composer's vendor tree and the
# dependency-ready marker run.sh drops.
testdata/legacy-api-v2/recorder/seat-api/
testdata/legacy-api-v2/recorder/seat-eveapi/
testdata/legacy-api-v2/recorder/seat-services/
testdata/legacy-api-v2/recorder/seat-web/
testdata/legacy-api-v2/recorder/vendor/
testdata/legacy-api-v2/recorder/.deps-ready
# record.php writes here, never over responses/ — the diff between the two is
# the review step, so the run output itself is not an artefact.
testdata/legacy-api-v2/recorder/out/

# ── local data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/data/
/tmp/
*.sqlite
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.bz2
!testdata/**/*.jsonl

# ── editors / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
